ar solid 5 layered mechanics create a  world in which we're always working  toward a goal whether it be new  equipment new allies or the means to  expand our home base  in the end though the phantom pain  excels because it reminds us that  everything is fleeting and we could be  moments away from losing it all fallout  4 is inhabitants on the other hand  already know that they wake each day to  a decaying world and pale son eking out  a living amidst the post nuclear waste  of Boston Massachusetts but that's the  story is one of moral choices and in  this world survival often means for  getting your principles fallout 4 is  superb not just because it's exciting  exploration based gameplay but because  that gameplay aligns with the setting we  roam its waist form Alliance and  scavenge for materials in the interest  of staying alive its crafting is superb  and deciding where to go next is half  the appeal of this game not just which  weapons to use or what armor to wear but  whether we would sacrifice our friends  for the good of the human race this  brings us to rise of the Tomb Raider a  game also steeped in moral ambiguity  Lara Croft is a video game icon but  developer Crystal Dynamics molds are  here to great effect in a story where  people's motives aren't as initially  seen on a gameplay level rise of the  tomb Raider's refined mechanics feel  superb and the pacing creates momentum  throughout the entire game exploration  leads to resources which lead to new  equipment which leads to new secrets in  previous areas then we have the titular  tombs which has some of the more clever  puzzles this year and like everything  else and rise of the Tomb Raider they're  worth doing and they're just fun as  their completion leaves two items in  make Lara's Trek easier in short rise of  the Tomb Raider is an excellent  action-adventure game with almost no  added weight and is propelled by a great  story in a gorgeous detailed world 2015  was a great year for games across e